  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7x-3 & x+8\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (x+8)-(-2)\\cdot (7x-3) \\\\  & =4x+32+14x-6 \\\\  & =18x+26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18x+26 & =0 \\\\ 18x & =-26 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{13}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
